#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/exception-handling.md:2
msgctxt "s-1408e071af20-0000"
msgid "Exception handling"
msgstr "Manejo de excepciones"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/exception-handling.md:6
msgctxt "s-d10a68f9b083-0001"
msgid ""
"Exception handling is a language feature for errors: raise a signal, unwind "
"the stack and let a handler deal with it. It exists to keep the normal path "
"of the code free of error checks. COBOL has an older, simpler form. "
"⟦CODE_0001⟧ runs when an arithmetic result does not fit the field, and the "
"field stays unchanged. In ⟦MACRO_0002⟧ that overflow *is* the stop rule: a "
"two-digit counter overflows on purpose, and the error branch ends the loop. "
"Errors as control flow work, but they hide the real design from the next "
"reader."
msgstr ""
"El manejo de excepciones es una función del lenguaje para tratar errores: "
"lanza una señal, desenrolla la pila y deja que un manejador se ocupe de "
"ella. Así el recorrido normal del código queda libre de comprobaciones de "
"errores. COBOL tiene una forma más antigua y sencilla. ⟦CODE_0001⟧ se "
"ejecuta cuando un resultado aritmético no cabe en el campo, que queda "
"intacto. En ⟦MACRO_0002⟧ ese desbordamiento *es* la regla de parada: un "
"contador de dos dígitos se desborda a propósito y la rama de error termina "
"el bucle. Usar errores como flujo de control funciona, pero le oculta el "
"diseño real al siguiente lector."

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/exception-handling.md:10
msgctxt "s-39d06b583bce-0002"
msgid ""
"Exceptions alter control flow by unwinding outward until a handler accepts "
"them"
msgstr ""
"Las excepciones alteran el flujo de control: desenrollan la pila hasta que "
"un manejador las acepta"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/exception-handling.md:11
msgctxt "s-c400a38b37a9-0003"
msgid ""
"A sequence diagram of three nested calls. The function main, which has a try"
" and catch, calls process, and process calls save. Save throws an exception."
" The exception does not return to process in the normal way. It passes "
"through process, which has no handler, so the rest of process is skipped. It"
" reaches main, where the catch block handles it. After the handler, normal "
"flow continues in main. The normal return statements of save and process "
"never run."
msgstr ""
"Diagrama de secuencia de tres llamadas anidadas. La función main, que tiene "
"un try y un catch, llama a process. A su vez, process llama a save. La "
"función save lanza una excepción. La excepción no vuelve a process por la "
"vía normal. Atraviesa process, que no tiene manejador, así que se omite el "
"resto de process. Llega a main, donde la maneja el bloque catch. Tras el "
"manejador, el flujo normal continúa en main. Las sentencias de retorno "
"normal de save y process nunca se ejecutan."

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/exception-handling.md:12
msgctxt "s-5f4590a28789-0004"
msgid "main: try and catch"
msgstr "main: try y catch"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/exception-handling.md:13
msgctxt "s-19ed40bf62c3-0005"
msgid "process"
msgstr "process"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/exception-handling.md:14
msgctxt "s-157dca92e425-0006"
msgid "save"
msgstr "save"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/exception-handling.md:15
msgctxt "s-7edb360f06ac-0007"
msgid "call"
msgstr "llamada"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/exception-handling.md:16
msgctxt "s-7edb360f06ac-0008"
msgid "call"
msgstr "llamada"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/exception-handling.md:17
msgctxt "s-59b780178acb-0009"
msgid "throws an exception"
msgstr "lanza una excepción"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/exception-handling.md:18
msgctxt "s-64ccaa3afa3d-0010"
msgid "unwinds, no normal return"
msgstr "desenrolla sin retorno normal"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/exception-handling.md:19
msgctxt "s-9a55f663b10d-0011"
msgid "no handler, the rest is skipped"
msgstr "sin manejador, se omite el resto"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/exception-handling.md:20
msgctxt "s-64ccaa3afa3d-0012"
msgid "unwinds, no normal return"
msgstr "desenrolla sin retorno normal"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/exception-handling.md:21
msgctxt "s-381593c489b2-0013"
msgid "catch block runs"
msgstr "se ejecuta el bloque catch"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/exception-handling.md:22
msgctxt "s-8f2d4885d825-0014"
msgid "normal flow resumes after the try"
msgstr "el flujo normal sigue tras el try"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/exception-handling.md:25
msgctxt "s-537466d290e0-0015"
msgid ""
"The normal ⟦CODE_0001⟧ of ⟦CODE_0002⟧ and ⟦CODE_0003⟧ never runs. The "
"exception passes outward through each call until a ⟦CODE_0004⟧ accepts it, "
"and then normal flow resumes after the ⟦CODE_0005⟧ in ⟦CODE_0006⟧. If "
"nothing catches it, it leaves the program. Unwinding only moves control. It "
"does not undo what the skipped code already did: a row that ⟦CODE_0007⟧ "
"wrote stays written, unless a transaction rolls it back (see ⟦MACRO_0008⟧)."
msgstr ""
"El ⟦CODE_0001⟧ normal de ⟦CODE_0002⟧ y ⟦CODE_0003⟧ nunca se ejecuta. La "
"excepción sale de cada llamada hasta que un ⟦CODE_0004⟧ la acepta. Entonces "
"el flujo normal se reanuda tras el ⟦CODE_0005⟧ en ⟦CODE_0006⟧. Si nada la "
"atrapa, sale del programa. Desenrollar la pila solo desplaza el control. No "
"deshace lo que ya hizo el código que se omite. Una fila que escribió "
"⟦CODE_0007⟧ queda escrita, salvo que una transacción revierta el cambio "
"(consulta ⟦MACRO_0008⟧)."

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/exception-handling.md:27
msgctxt "s-382e961801c1-0016"
msgid ""
"**Use it when:** something truly unexpected happens, and the caller can "
"recover or must be told."
msgstr ""
"**Úsalo cuando:** ocurra algo realmente inesperado y quien llama pueda "
"recuperarse o deba enterarse."

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/exception-handling.md:28
msgctxt "s-e39a7a33f58a-0017"
msgid ""
"**Avoid it when:** the \"error\" is a normal, frequent outcome (such as "
"\"end of input\"), or when you catch everything and move on in silence."
msgstr ""
"**Evítalo cuando:** el \"error\" sea un resultado normal y frecuente (como "
"\"fin de la entrada de datos\") o cuando atrapes todo y sigas sin avisar."

